      "explanation": "The doctor never achieves safe bounded closure. The final message is an open-ended, non-executable plan for the family. There is no distinction between what has been safely organized for today and what remains as unresolved, tracked residual risk. The closure is not safe, executable, or traceable.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "The doctor never helps the family manage staged information return, caregiver disagreement, or limited access to busy ICU clinicians with a practical coordination method. There is no proposal for a written tracking structure, a family spokesperson, or a fallback route through the bedside nurse.",
